<UserControl x:Class="ConditioningControlPanel.Views.Tabs.StudioTabView"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:loc="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Localization"
             xmlns:helpers="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Helpers"
             xmlns:feat="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Features"
             xmlns:studio="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Views.Controls.Studio"
             xmlns:tabs="clr-namespace:ConditioningControlPanel.Views.Tabs"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             d:DesignHeight="700" d:DesignWidth="1460">

    <!-- ========================================================================
         THE STUDIO DOOR (UX restructure, Phase 4 · tab key "studio")

         The effects rack: a fixed left list of modules, a detail pane on the
         right showing exactly ONE module. It replaces the thirteen
         FeaturePopupWindow openers as the primary home for the per-feature
         config panels - the popups still exist and still work (the dashboard
         mosaic keeps opening them), because a popup builds its OWN fresh
         instance every time and nothing here is ever re-parented.

         WHY THE PANELS ARE ALL INSTANTIATED HERE, ALWAYS (ground rule §2.3):
         no lazy creation. Every Features/*FeatureControl below is constructed
         with this view and toggled by Visibility, exactly like the tab views
         themselves. Their Loaded/Unloaded pairs subscribe/unsubscribe
         AppSettings.PropertyChanged symmetrically, so thirteen permanently
         live INPC listeners is the whole cost.

         WHY NOTHING IS RE-PARENTED: a UserControl has exactly one visual
         parent. The rack owning an instance AND a popup borrowing it is the
         DetachWebcamBarInto mechanism Phase 2 just deleted; it fires
         Unloaded/Loaded, which re-runs LoadFromSettings and re-subscribes
         handlers. Two independent instances that both re-read App.Settings on
         PropertyChanged stay in step for free.

         HAPTICS LIVES HERE NOW. HapticsTabView (1353 lines, its own page) was
         a top-level tab mounted in MainWindow.xaml; it moved into this rack
         WHOLE, not decomposed. MainWindow keeps reaching it through a single
         MainWindow.HapticsTab passthrough (MainWindow.TabNavigation.cs), so
         all 71 `HapticsTab.<x:Name>` dereferences across the MainWindow
         partials, the two features/vibe.png repaint rows, the
         IsVisibleChanged live-status hook and the SessionLock sweep keep
         working untouched. ShowTab("haptics") still fires the bark key
         "haptics", never "studio".

         QUIET SURFACE (PLAN §2.7, hard rule 7): no ambient loop is registered
         for this view and none may be. The rack's selection visual is trigger
         driven - no clock, nothing for the motion kill-switch to reach. The
         only motion is a 120ms detail crossfade, gated on MotionFx.

         RESOURCES: a UserControl's XAML is parsed before it is attached to
         MainWindow, so a StaticResource declared in MainWindow.xaml's own
         Resources will NOT resolve here. Everything below comes from
         Resources/Theme/*.xaml or the local Resources block (Phase 2 lesson).
         ======================================================================== -->

    <UserControl.Resources>

        <!-- Rack row. Same grammar as the nav rail's active indicator and the
             Settings door's section pills: a 3px accent bar plus a tinted fill,
             both driven by ControlTemplate triggers. Deliberately no storyboard -
             a trigger setter is not an animation, so there is nothing here for
             MotionFx to gate or for the kill-switch to stop. -->
        <Style x:Key="RackEntryStyle" TargetType="RadioButton">
            <Setter Property="GroupName" Value="StudioRack"/>
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12.5"/>
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand"/>
            <Setter Property="Focusable" Value="True"/>
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,1"/>
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch"/>
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="RadioButton">
                        <Grid Background="Transparent" Height="30">
                            <Border x:Name="RowFill" CornerRadius="8" Opacity="0"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource TransparentPink20Brush}"/>
                            <Border x:Name="RowBar" Width="3" CornerRadius="2" Margin="0,5"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Left" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource PinkBrush}"/>
                            <ContentPresenter Margin="12,0,10,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </Grid>
                        <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                            <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                                <Setter TargetName="RowFill" Property="Opacity" Value="0.5"/>
                                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}"/>
                            </Trigger>
                            <Trigger Property="IsChecked" Value="True">
                                <Setter TargetName="RowFill" Property="Opacity" Value="1"/>
                                <Setter TargetName="RowBar" Property="Visibility" Value="Visible"/>
                                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextLightBrush}"/>
                                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
                            </Trigger>
                        </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

    </UserControl.Resources>

    <Grid>
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ============================ page header ============================ -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" Margin="4,2,4,12">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Image Grid.Column="0" Width="30" Height="30" Margin="0,0,12,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality"
                   Source="pack://application:,,,/Resources/nav/door_studio.png">
                <Image.Clip>
                    <RectangleGeometry Rect="0,0,30,30" RadiusX="8" RadiusY="8"/>
                </Image.Clip>
            </Image>
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <TextBlock x:Name="TxtStudioTitle" Text="{loc:Str st4_studio_title}"
                           Foreground="White" FontSize="21" FontWeight="Bold"/>
                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Str st4_studio_subtitle}"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMutedBrush}" FontSize="12.5"/>
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ========================== rack + detail pane ======================== -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="1">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

            <!-- The rack list. Fixed 230 wide per the Phase-4 contract; rows are built in
                 code from the single RackEntries table so the key, the icon, the label, the
                 state dot, the panel and the NotifyFeatureOpened key can never drift apart. -->
            <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="230" Margin="0,0,14,0"
                    Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceBgBrush}" BorderBrush="#2A2A46"
                    BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="12" Padding="8,10">
                <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
                    <StackPanel x:Name="RackList"/>
                </ScrollViewer>
            </Border>

            <!-- The detail column. -->
            <Grid Grid.Column="1">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                    <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- Stand-in for the FeaturePopupWindow title bar: same icon + title the popup
                     showed, so a panel that used to name itself in a window chrome still does.
                     Collapsed for modules that draw their own page header (Haptics). -->
                <Border x:Name="DetailHeader" Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,10" Padding="14,9"
                        Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceBgBrush}" BorderBrush="#2A2A46"
                        BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="10">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                        <helpers:EmojiTextBlock x:Name="TxtDetailIcon" FontSize="15"
                                                VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,9,0"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="TxtDetailTitle" Foreground="White" FontSize="14"
                                   FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <!-- Every module's panel, all instantiated, exactly one visible.

                     Each Features/* panel gets its OWN ScrollViewer and ~14px of padding
                     because that is what FeaturePopupWindow gave it (ScrollViewer Padding=16
                     inside a fixed 520x640 window); without it the long panels - Flash 255
                     XAML lines, BouncingText 246, System 228, Spiral 226 - clip silently with
                     no scrollbar at all (fx-inventory §12.8).

                     HapticsTabView is the exception: its own root IS a ScrollViewer, so it is
                     hosted raw. Nesting it would give it infinite available height and it
                     would never scroll. -->
                <Grid x:Name="DetailHost" Grid.Row="1">

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostFlash" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:FlashFeatureControl x:Name="PanelFlash"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostVisuals" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:VisualsFeatureControl x:Name="PanelVisuals"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostVideo" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:VideoFeatureControl x:Name="PanelVideo"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostSubliminal" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:SubliminalFeatureControl x:Name="PanelSubliminal"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostSpiral" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:SpiralFeatureControl x:Name="PanelSpiral"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostPinkFilter" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:PinkFilterFeatureControl x:Name="PanelPinkFilter"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <!-- TxtTriggerEggHint travels with this panel (preservation item 15). KNOWN
                         GAP: it is set in BubblePopFeatureControl.LoadFromSettings, which only
                         runs on Loaded and on flash/bubble property changes - so on this
                         long-lived instance the persona name ("careful — Bambi loves these…")
                         goes stale after a mod switch until a bubble setting moves. The fix
                         belongs in the panel or in ApplyModFeatureNames, not here; see
                         CONCERNS in the Phase-4 handoff. -->
                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostBubblePop" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:BubblePopFeatureControl x:Name="PanelBubblePop"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostLockCard" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:LockCardFeatureControl x:Name="PanelLockCard"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostBubbleCount" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:BubbleCountFeatureControl x:Name="PanelBubbleCount"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostBouncingText" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:BouncingTextFeatureControl x:Name="PanelBouncingText"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostMindWipe" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <feat:MindWipeFeatureControl x:Name="PanelMindWipe"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <!-- NEW in Phase 4 (Views/Controls/Studio/, built by the Brain Drain agent).
                         G2 rescue: the controls existed ONLY in the dead ProgressionTabView XAML
                         with no handlers attached. OverlayService.BrainDrainWithheld is FALSE
                         since the rework shipped: the blur half is live on the compositor and the
                         panel carries its blur-strength slider + melt toggle. -->
                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostBrainDrain" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <studio:BrainDrainFeatureControl x:Name="PanelBrainDrain"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <!-- SystemFeatureControl and AppInfoFeatureControl are deliberately NOT rack
                         modules (Phase-4 contract): System is configuration + the No-Panic
                         safety control, and both belong to the Settings/Home doors. The
                         dashboard's System tile keeps opening its popup, so the
                         NotifyFeatureOpened("System") bark rule keeps firing from there. -->

                    <!-- Hosted RAW: HapticsTabView's root is already a ScrollViewer (and it
                         carries its own 34px page header, which is why DetailHeader hides for
                         this module). MainWindow.HapticsTab passthrough points here. -->
                    <tabs:HapticsTabView x:Name="PanelHaptics" Visibility="Collapsed"/>

                    <!-- NEW in Phase 4 (Views/Controls/Studio/). These wrap the LIVE
                         Features/SchedulerFeatureControl and Features/IntensityRampFeatureControl -
                         NOT the strictly-poorer dead twins in ProgressionTabView (which lack
                         CmbRampCurve). MainWindow.Settings.cs still SAVES the schedule from the
                         ProgressionTab copies, so nothing about those may be deleted in Phase 4. -->
                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostScheduler" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <studio:SchedulerRackPanel x:Name="PanelScheduler"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <ScrollViewer x:Name="HostRamp" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                                  Padding="2,0,14,10">
                        <studio:RampRackPanel x:Name="PanelRamp"/>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                </Grid>
            </Grid>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
